  mechanism. A 2-bit confidence counter is added to each RDP entry, trained by
  the sampler on reuse (increment) and eviction/timeout (decrement). Lines with
  low-confidence reuse predictions (confidence < 2) are given an ETR penalty (+2),
  making them more likely eviction candidates. This aims to reduce `kept_dead`
  mistakes by being more skeptical of uncertain predictions, while retaining the
  performance benefits of faster learning.
  This update modifies the bypass conditions to also require high confidence
  in RDP predictions for the incoming line. Specifically, both bypass conditions
  now check that the `rdp_confidence` for the incoming line's `pc_sig` is at least 2,
