name: mj_correct_conf_and_evict
doc: >
  Corrects the inverted confidence training logic from the parent, which caused
  high kept_dead and should_bypass errors. Confidence in a line being 'dead' is
  now correctly learned: incremented on eviction without reuse, and decremented
  on reuse. This corrected confidence is used to make bypass decisions more
  accurate. Also adds a rule to mark lines confidently predicted as dead for
  immediate eviction, tackling the kept_dead issue. Restores sampler ways from 4
  to 5 to improve predictor accuracy, which fits within the memory budget.

